abstract: >-
  A governance evidence engine for machine-learning-based small business
  credit underwriting. It maintains structured model and version records,
  evaluates configured monitoring thresholds, generates and reviews
  adverse-action reasons for accuracy and traceability under Regulation B
  12 CFR 1002.9, runs model-change and validation review, and assembles
  reviewer-ready evidence packs with input and output fingerprints. It
  ships deterministic synthetic fixtures and a public-data run kit for
  fixed-horizon, out-of-time model-risk monitoring. Fair-lending screening
  with statistical significance testing, BISG protected-class proxy
  estimation, and less-discriminatory-alternative assessment are included
  as supporting risk-management components.
